# Realme Buds Desktop — Implementation Plan

A desktop application to control **Realme Buds T310** ANC modes (Noise Canceling, Transparent, **Normal**) from Windows, solving the problem that "Normal" mode is locked behind the mobile-only Realme Link app.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Phase 1 (Protocol Discovery) requires your hands-on work** before any code can be written. You need to capture Bluetooth traffic from your Android phone while using the Realme Link app. Without the discovered hex commands, the app cannot send the right bytes to your earbuds.

> [!WARNING]
> **Technology Choice Decision Needed**: I'm recommending **Electron** for the desktop shell because it has mature Web Bluetooth support and a large ecosystem. An alternative is **Tauri** (Rust-based, smaller binary) with `tauri-plugin-blec`. Electron is easier to get started with; Tauri produces a ~5MB app vs Electron's ~80MB. **Which do you prefer?**

---

