## Phase 3: Configuration & Protocol File

#### [NEW] [src/protocol/realme-t310.json](file:///c:/Users/Admin/Documents/pc_doc/realme-buds-desktop/realme-buds-desktop/src/protocol/realme-t310.json)

Stores the discovered protocol data — this gets populated after Phase 1:

```json
{
  "device_name": "realme Buds T310",
  "service_uuid": "TO_BE_DISCOVERED",
  "characteristic_uuid": "TO_BE_DISCOVERED",
  "commands": {
    "noise_canceling": "TO_BE_DISCOVERED",
    "transparent": "TO_BE_DISCOVERED",
    "normal": "TO_BE_DISCOVERED"
  },
  "handshake": null
}
```

This separation means **adding support for other Realme earbuds later** just requires adding a new JSON file.

---

## Phase 4: System Tray & Auto-Connect

- Minimize to system tray with context menu for quick mode switching
- Auto-connect to last known device on app startup
- Keyboard shortcuts for mode switching

---

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests

Since this project involves hardware (Bluetooth earbuds), automated testing is limited to unit-testing the protocol layer:

```bash
# Run unit tests for command building / protocol parsing
npm test
```

Tests will cover:
- Protocol JSON loading and validation
- Command byte construction
- IPC message formatting

### Manual Verification (User Required)

> [!IMPORTANT]
> Hardware testing requires the actual earbuds. I cannot verify BLE communication without them.

| # | Test | Steps | Expected Result |
|---|------|-------|----------------|
| 1 | **App launches** | Run `npm run dev` | Electron window opens with dark UI |
| 2 | **Device scan** | Click "Scan" button | T310 appears in device list |
| 3 | **Connect** | Click on T310 in list | Status shows "Connected", battery level appears |
| 4 | **Switch to Normal** | Click "Normal" button | Earbuds switch to Normal mode (no ANC, no transparency) |
| 5 | **Switch to ANC** | Click "ANC" button | Earbuds activate noise canceling |
| 6 | **Switch to Transparent** | Click "Transparent" button | Earbuds activate transparency mode |
| 7 | **System tray** | Minimize app | Tray icon appears, right-click shows mode options |
| 8 | **Reconnect** | Restart app with earbuds on | Auto-connects to T310 |

### Python Bleak Quick-Test Script (For Protocol Discovery Phase)

Before building the full Electron app, we'll create a simple Python script to quickly validate discovered commands:

```bash
# Install bleak
pip install bleak

# Run the test script
python scripts/test_connection.py
```

This script will:
1. Scan for the T310
2. Connect and list all GATT services/characteristics  
3. Try sending the discovered command bytes
4. Report which mode the earbuds switched to
